simple patterns (vocab=256, len=4096, n=200/pattern):
  uniform baseline ln(V) = 5.5452 nats   (an unstructured iid sequence is irreducible at this value)

  pattern                 pad%   floor  unigram  gzip  floor/lnV
  --------------------------------------------------------------
  periodic                  0%  0.0055   5.3322  0.01      0.001
  palindrome                0%  2.7726   5.5410  1.01      0.500
  copy                      0%  2.3475   5.5415  0.44      0.423
  reverse                   0%  2.7733   5.5419  1.01      0.500
  counting_anbn             0%  0.1666   5.1809  0.08      0.030
  counting_anbncn           0%  0.1134   5.3051  0.08      0.020
  nested                    0%  2.7726   5.5410  1.01      0.500
  interleaving              0%  0.0027   5.1394  0.01      0.000
  permutation_cycle         0%  0.0047   5.2989  0.01      0.001
  hierarchical              0%  0.0041   5.2443  0.01      0.001
  noisy_palindrome*         0%  3.2759   5.5410  1.01      0.591
  random                    0%  5.5452   5.5411  1.01      1.000
  identity                  0%  0.0014   4.7662  0.01      0.000
  composite_mirror_repeat    0%  1.3863   5.5407  0.52      0.250
  mixer*                    0%  1.2988   5.5367  0.47      0.234  <- PAD INSIDE BODY!

  Legend:
    pad%      : fraction of tokens that are the reserved masked pad (ID 0; excluded from the loss)
    floor     : min achievable mean loss over UNMASKED tokens (the true training floor)
    unigram   : naive global-unigram cross-entropy (memorization baseline)
    gzip      : mean gzip compression ratio (README complexity metric)
    floor/lnV : floor as a fraction of the uniform baseline (0 = fully predictable, 1 = unstructured)
    *         : floor is a LOOSE lower bound (true floor is higher); counting_* use a dedicated EXACT oracle

